The Following is a list of ToolTypes for this ICON:


NOTICE: ALL TOOLTYPES ARE CASE SENSITIVE

ABOUT: This ICON is required in each NODE directory. It specifies the
       window dimensions for the NODE.


WINDOW.LEFTEDGE=
WINDOW.TOPEDGE=
WINDOW.HEIGHT=
WINDOW.WIDTH=
WINDOW.NUM_COLORS=
WINDOW.STATBAR
WINDOW.ICONIFIED
WINDOW.INTERLACE


WINDOW.LEFTEDGE=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express the left edge coordinates for the NODE window in
          screen pixels.

     WINDOW.LEFTEDGE=0


WINDOW.TOPEDGE=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express the top edge coordinates for the NODE window in
          screen pixels.

     WINDOW.TOPEDGE=0


WINDOW.HEIGHT=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express the Height in pixels that the NODE window should be.

     WINDOW.HEIGHT=200


WINDOW.WIDTH=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express the width in pixels that the NODE window should be.

     WINDOW.WIDTH=200


WINDOW.NUM_COLORS=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express the number of colors allowed for the NODE window.
         -If 0 colors are specified, then express will open the window on
          the workbench screen.

     WINDOW.NUM_COLORS=8


WINDOW.STATBAR

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express that you wish a Status Window to open on the NODE
          window, which reflects detailed account infomation on users as
          they logon.

     WINDOW.STATBAR


WINDOW.ICONIFIED

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express that you do not want the window open on startup of
          the NODE.

     WINDOW.ICONIFIED


WINDOW.INTERLACE

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express that the NODE window will be in INTERLACE mode.

     WINDOW.INTERLACE

WINDOW.TO_FRONT

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells express to bring the NODE SCREEN to the Front of all other
          Screens active on the System.

     WINDOW.TO_FRONT


